The Security Council,

Recalling the purposes and principles of the Charter of the United Nations, including the sovereignty, political independence, territorial integrity and non-interference in the internal affairs of all States,

Reaffirming its primary responsibility for the maintenance of international peace and security,

Expressing grave concern at the deteriorating humanitarian situation in the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela, including shortages of food, medicine and basic services, and its impact on the civilian population, especially children, women, older persons and vulnerable groups,

Expressing grave concern at the violence and loss of life, including at the borders, and at reports of human rights violations and abuses, and stressing the need for the protection of civilians and for accountability,

Stressing the need for a peaceful and negotiated solution to the political crisis in the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela through inclusive dialogue and democratic processes, and reaffirming the importance of free, fair, transparent and credible elections in accordance with the Venezuelan Constitution,

Stressing that humanitarian assistance should be provided in accordance with the humanitarian principles of humanity, neutrality, impartiality and independence, and the guiding principles of United Nations humanitarian assistance,

Expressing deep concern at reports of the obstruction of the delivery of humanitarian assistance, and recalling the obligation of all parties to respect and protect humanitarian personnel and to allow safe and unhindered access,

Recognizing the efforts of neighbouring countries and regional organizations to provide humanitarian assistance and to promote peaceful dialogue,

Welcoming the efforts of the Secretary-General to use his good offices and reaffirming the importance of respect for human rights and fundamental freedoms,

Emphasizing the need for all parties to refrain from violence and to protect civilians, and deeply concerned by the risk of further escalation and its humanitarian consequences,

1. Calls upon all parties in the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela to immediately cease violence, refrain from acts that could escalate tensions and ensure the safety and protection of civilians;

2. Calls upon all parties to allow and facilitate safe, rapid and unimpeded access for humanitarian assistance to all parts of the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela, and to ensure that humanitarian assistance is provided in accordance with humanitarian principles;

3. Calls upon all Member States and international organizations to provide humanitarian assistance to the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela in response to the crisis, and encourages the Secretary-General to coordinate with relevant humanitarian actors;

4. Encourages an inclusive and credible political dialogue among all Venezuelan actors, in accordance with the Venezuelan Constitution, to find a peaceful solution to the crisis, including through free, fair, transparent and credible elections;

5. Calls for full respect for human rights, fundamental freedoms and the rule of law, and for the protection of all persons, including humanitarian personnel, and for accountability for violations and abuses;

6. Reaffirms its respect for the sovereignty, political independence and territorial integrity of the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela and the principle of non-interference in its internal affairs;

7. Requests the Secretary-General to use his good offices to facilitate dialogue and humanitarian assistance, and to report to the Security Council on the implementation of this resolution within 30 days;

8. Decides to remain actively seized of the matter.

